Let an element opt out of touch-to-mouse emulation with `on_touch`, and deliver taps as `ClickEvent::Touch`.

What: `TouchEvent` becomes a `MouseEvent`, so `Window::on_mouse_event` can listen for raw touches. The window sends
each started touch to those listeners while its route is `TouchRoute::Deciding`; the first listener to decide wins,
and bubble order visits the frontmost element first, so the deepest handler under the touch decides (Flutter's
gesture arena, simplified):
- `Window::claim_touch(touch, owner)` routes it to `TouchRoute::Claimed(GlobalElementId)`. Every later phase is
  dispatched to touch listeners, which check `Window::touch_owner`, so it reaches the owner even after the owner moves
  between frames. It never reaches the gesture recognizer: no mouse press, click, scroll or long press.
- Elements with tap, press, drag or scroll handlers leave it to the recognizer (`TouchRoute::Gestures`), as does
  nobody deciding. So a button inside an `on_touch` canvas still clicks, and a scroll container inside it scrolls.
The started touch is hit-tested at its position without moving the window's mouse position for good. After a claimed
touch ends, the window draws if dirty, as it already does after a tap, so the platform's release handler (web: virtual
keyboard) sees input handlers that match a focus change the listener made.

`StatefulInteractiveElement::on_touch` / `Interactivity::on_touch` is the element API: it claims touches that start
over the element when nothing deeper decided. It needs an element id (like `on_click`): the claim names the element.

Separately, div's click handling now builds the declared `ClickEvent::Touch(TouchClickEvent)` when the press and
release were synthesized from a tap (per `Window::pointer_source()`, patch 0003), so `on_click` listeners can tell
taps from clicks.

Why: upstream synthesizes mouse events for every tap and gives elements no raw touches (the `TouchEvent` docs call
per-touch dispatch "pending"), and `ClickEvent::Touch` is declared but never built. Drawing surfaces, sliders and
custom gestures need raw touches without a stray click or scroll.

Depends on: 0003 (`Window::pointer_source`; `PointerDevice` in tests).

Test: `touch_listeners_opt_an_element_out_of_touch_to_mouse` (div.rs): one row per element tree and gesture (tap,
pan, mouse click; canvas alone, button inside a canvas, canvas inside a canvas, scroller inside a canvas, a thumb that
follows the finger), also checking the post-release draw and the mouse position.

Size: ~400 added lines, ~230 of them the test table and its fixture; the code is ~170.

Upstream PR: not filed yet.

